{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1t1JSkui7feW1mcDTPezV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — exec-sim-repair-verifier\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Extended fallback: ICSE 2027 (Jun 23 abstract, Jun 30 paper)\n7\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (9 days remaining)\n8\t\n9\t## D116 Framing Pivot (2026-05-16)\n10\t\n11\t**前 framing**: \"CLS scales where generation fails\" (CLS advocacy)\n12\t**新 framing**: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n13\t\n14\t核心转变：不再主张任何 formulation 普遍更好，而是 characterize 何时用什么。\n15\t最强贡献重新定位：\n16\t1. CWM 失败模式是 **tokenizer/model-specific** 而非 formulation-inherent（Qwen 93% unparseable vs DeepSeek 11.8%）\n17\t2. Error complementarity: CLS/CWM 有系统性互补错误模式，oracle ensemble +2-3pp\n18\t3. 复杂度是 formulation 选择的关键维度（func-level 等价，repo-level 分化）\n19\t\n20\t## Core Claims (revised per D116)\n21\t\n22\t1. **Formulation Equivalence at Low Complexity**: At function-level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ achieve statistically equivalent accuracy across two model families (Qwen3: 88.4/87.2/86.3%; DeepSeek: 86.9/86.8/84.2%). Formulation choice does not matter when execution outputs are short and structured.\n23\t\n24\t2. **Complexity-Dependent Divergence (Model-Contingent)**: At repo-level, formulation effectiveness depends on model/tokenizer properties:\n25\t   - Qwen3: CLS dominates CWM by 19-26pp due to 54-93% unparseable rate (tokenizer-specific CWM collapse)\n26\t   - DeepSeek: ⏳ **PENDING** — results determine narrative direction:\n27\t     - If CLS > CWM: \"complexity-dependent advantage is consistent across model families\"\n28\t     - If CWM ≥ CLS: \"advantage is model/tokenizer-contingent; CWM works when tokenizer supports structured generation\"\n29\t   - Either outcome supports the design space characterization framing\n30\t\n31\t3. **Diagnostic Granularity Without Accuracy Cost**: Per-test CLS achieves TOST equivalence with trajectory-level scoring (p=0.007, ±2pp margin, Qwen3) while providing per-test failure localization. Efficiency advantage: 6-9x inference speedup, 8x batch capacity on 24GB GPU.\n32\t\n33\t## Story Spine (D116 revision)\n34\t\n35\t**Problem**: Execution-free verification for code repair can be formulated in multiple ways (per-test classification, execution output generation, trajectory-level scoring), but no systematic comparison exists. Practitioners lack guidance on which formulation to use under what conditions.\n36\t\n37\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Code World Models generate execution outputs but suffer from format compliance failures at scale. Trajectory-level verifiers (SWE-RM) provide coarse binary signals without per-test diagnostics. Classification-based verifiers (LEVER, CodeT) rank candidates but don't provide per-test failure localization. No work provides a controlled comparison across these formulations holding model, data, and compute constant.\n38\t\n39\t**Our contribution**: We present the first controlled comparison of three verification formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) across 2 model families, 2 complexity levels, and multiple seeds. Key findings:\n40\t1. Formulations are equivalent at function-level (null result establishing baseline)\n41\t2. Formulations diverge at repo-level in a model-contingent manner\n42\t3. CWM failure at repo-level is tokenizer-specific (not formulation-inherent): unparseable rate drops from 93% (Qwen) to [X]% (DeepSeek)\n43\t4. CLS and CWM exhibit complementary error patterns (oracle ensemble: 90.63%)\n44\t5. Per-test CLS matches trajectory-level accuracy while providing diagnostic granularity at 6-9x lower inference cost\n45\t\n46\t**Headline result template (dual-path)**:\n47\t- Path A (CLS > CWM on DeepSeek): \"Classification consistently outperforms generation at repo-level across model families, but the magnitude depends on tokenizer-specific format compliance. We characterize when and why each formulation succeeds.\"\n48\t- Path B (CWM ≥ CLS on DeepSeek): \"No single formulation dominates: CLS wins on Qwen (tokenizer-induced CWM collapse) while CWM matches/exceeds CLS on DeepSeek. The formulation design space is model-contingent, and we provide the empirical characterization needed to navigate it.\"\n49\t\n50\t## Venue Fit Risks\n51\t\n52\t1. **Novelty concern (Dream consensus)**: \"Classification > generation when outputs are complex\" is predictable. Mitigation: novelty is in (a) empirical demonstration that it's tokenizer-specific not formulation-inherent, (b) error complementarity analysis, (c) systematic controlled comparison methodology. Frame as \"empirical characterization with actionable insights\" not \"method contribution.\"\n53\t\n54\t2. **EMNLP vs SE venue**: Mitigation: (a) process vs outcome supervision parallel (Lightman et al., 2023; Uesato et al., 2022), (b) general NLP methodology insight about classification vs generation.\n55\t\n56\t3. **CWM comparison fairness**: Original CWM is 32B with mid-training on execution traces; we compare 4-8B LoRA. Mitigation: explicitly scope as \"same-size LoRA comparison\" and discuss that generation may need more capacity. This limitation actually strengthens the practical guidance: \"at practical deployment sizes (4-8B), classification is the safer choice.\"\n57\t\n58\t4. **Re-repair null result**: Downstream utility unvalidated. Mitigation: frame efficiency + diagnostic granularity as the practical benefit, not re-repair. Re-repair is future work.\n59\t\n60\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigations (updated per Dream)\n61\t\n62\t| Concern | Mitigation |\n63\t|---------|------------|\n64\t| \"Limited novelty — obvious that classification is easier\" | Func-level null result proves it's NOT trivially easier; advantage is complexity+tokenizer-dependent. Strongest novelty: CWM failure is tokenizer-specific |\n65\t| \"CWM comparison unfair (4-8B LoRA vs 32B full)\" | Explicitly scope as same-size comparison; discuss scale as limitation; practical guidance framing |\n66\t| \"Single-seed repo-level\" | Multi-seed replication (2 seeds × 2 formulations × DeepSeek, running) |\n67\t| \"Cross-model validation incomplete\" | DeepSeek repo experiments (running); whichever direction supports the design space characterization |\n68\t| \"No downstream utility\" | Efficiency benefit (6-9x) is practical; re-repair honestly framed as future work |\n69\t| \"Claims outrun evidence\" | D116: remove all advocacy language; report what evidence supports, nothing more |\n70\t| \"Process vs outcome supervision parallel\" | Add Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 to Related Work |\n71\t\n72\t## Related Work Additions Needed (Dream feedback)\n73\t- Process vs outcome supervision: Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 (CLS vs TRAJ parallel)\n74\t- CodeRL, AlphaCode, Reflexion (verification-in-the-loop repair)\n75\t- Predictive mutation testing literature (per-test binary classification precedent)\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a235da8-f9b2-40e9-885f-aa66b75ac7cf","uuid":"0e41f8fa-3e00-4db2-bf71-153f7f819642","timestamp":"2026-05-17T03:54:27.078Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T034206/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — exec-sim-repair-verifier\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Extended fallback: ICSE 2027 (Jun 23 abstract, Jun 30 paper)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (9 days remaining)\n\n## D116 Framing Pivot (2026-05-16)\n\n**前 framing**: \"CLS scales where generation fails\" (CLS advocacy)\n**新 framing**: \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" (empirical characterization)\n\n核心转变：不再主张任何 formulation 普遍更好，而是 characterize 何时用什么。\n最强贡献重新定位：\n1. CWM 失败模式是 **tokenizer/model-specific** 而非 formulation-inherent（Qwen 93% unparseable vs DeepSeek 11.8%）\n2. Error complementarity: CLS/CWM 有系统性互补错误模式，oracle ensemble +2-3pp\n3. 复杂度是 formulation 选择的关键维度（func-level 等价，repo-level 分化）\n\n## Core Claims (revised per D116)\n\n1. **Formulation Equivalence at Low Complexity**: At function-level, CLS, CWM, and TRAJ achieve statistically equivalent accuracy across two model families (Qwen3: 88.4/87.2/86.3%; DeepSeek: 86.9/86.8/84.2%). Formulation choice does not matter when execution outputs are short and structured.\n\n2. **Complexity-Dependent Divergence (Model-Contingent)**: At repo-level, formulation effectiveness depends on model/tokenizer properties:\n   - Qwen3: CLS dominates CWM by 19-26pp due to 54-93% unparseable rate (tokenizer-specific CWM collapse)\n   - DeepSeek: ⏳ **PENDING** — results determine narrative direction:\n     - If CLS > CWM: \"complexity-dependent advantage is consistent across model families\"\n     - If CWM ≥ CLS: \"advantage is model/tokenizer-contingent; CWM works when tokenizer supports structured generation\"\n   - Either outcome supports the design space characterization framing\n\n3. **Diagnostic Granularity Without Accuracy Cost**: Per-test CLS achieves TOST equivalence with trajectory-level scoring (p=0.007, ±2pp margin, Qwen3) while providing per-test failure localization. Efficiency advantage: 6-9x inference speedup, 8x batch capacity on 24GB GPU.\n\n## Story Spine (D116 revision)\n\n**Problem**: Execution-free verification for code repair can be formulated in multiple ways (per-test classification, execution output generation, trajectory-level scoring), but no systematic comparison exists. Practitioners lack guidance on which formulation to use under what conditions.\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Code World Models generate execution outputs but suffer from format compliance failures at scale. Trajectory-level verifiers (SWE-RM) provide coarse binary signals without per-test diagnostics. Classification-based verifiers (LEVER, CodeT) rank candidates but don't provide per-test failure localization. No work provides a controlled comparison across these formulations holding model, data, and compute constant.\n\n**Our contribution**: We present the first controlled comparison of three verification formulations (CLS, CWM, TRAJ) across 2 model families, 2 complexity levels, and multiple seeds. Key findings:\n1. Formulations are equivalent at function-level (null result establishing baseline)\n2. Formulations diverge at repo-level in a model-contingent manner\n3. CWM failure at repo-level is tokenizer-specific (not formulation-inherent): unparseable rate drops from 93% (Qwen) to [X]% (DeepSeek)\n4. CLS and CWM exhibit complementary error patterns (oracle ensemble: 90.63%)\n5. Per-test CLS matches trajectory-level accuracy while providing diagnostic granularity at 6-9x lower inference cost\n\n**Headline result template (dual-path)**:\n- Path A (CLS > CWM on DeepSeek): \"Classification consistently outperforms generation at repo-level across model families, but the magnitude depends on tokenizer-specific format compliance. We characterize when and why each formulation succeeds.\"\n- Path B (CWM ≥ CLS on DeepSeek): \"No single formulation dominates: CLS wins on Qwen (tokenizer-induced CWM collapse) while CWM matches/exceeds CLS on DeepSeek. The formulation design space is model-contingent, and we provide the empirical characterization needed to navigate it.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n1. **Novelty concern (Dream consensus)**: \"Classification > generation when outputs are complex\" is predictable. Mitigation: novelty is in (a) empirical demonstration that it's tokenizer-specific not formulation-inherent, (b) error complementarity analysis, (c) systematic controlled comparison methodology. Frame as \"empirical characterization with actionable insights\" not \"method contribution.\"\n\n2. **EMNLP vs SE venue**: Mitigation: (a) process vs outcome supervision parallel (Lightman et al., 2023; Uesato et al., 2022), (b) general NLP methodology insight about classification vs generation.\n\n3. **CWM comparison fairness**: Original CWM is 32B with mid-training on execution traces; we compare 4-8B LoRA. Mitigation: explicitly scope as \"same-size LoRA comparison\" and discuss that generation may need more capacity. This limitation actually strengthens the practical guidance: \"at practical deployment sizes (4-8B), classification is the safer choice.\"\n\n4. **Re-repair null result**: Downstream utility unvalidated. Mitigation: frame efficiency + diagnostic granularity as the practical benefit, not re-repair. Re-repair is future work.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Mitigations (updated per Dream)\n\n| Concern | Mitigation |\n|---------|------------|\n| \"Limited novelty — obvious that classification is easier\" | Func-level null result proves it's NOT trivially easier; advantage is complexity+tokenizer-dependent. Strongest novelty: CWM failure is tokenizer-specific |\n| \"CWM comparison unfair (4-8B LoRA vs 32B full)\" | Explicitly scope as same-size comparison; discuss scale as limitation; practical guidance framing |\n| \"Single-seed repo-level\" | Multi-seed replication (2 seeds × 2 formulations × DeepSeek, running) |\n| \"Cross-model validation incomplete\" | DeepSeek repo experiments (running); whichever direction supports the design space characterization |\n| \"No downstream utility\" | Efficiency benefit (6-9x) is practical; re-repair honestly framed as future work |\n| \"Claims outrun evidence\" | D116: remove all advocacy language; report what evidence supports, nothing more |\n| \"Process vs outcome supervision parallel\" | Add Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 to Related Work |\n\n## Related Work Additions Needed (Dream feedback)\n- Process vs outcome supervision: Lightman et al. 2023, Uesato et al. 2022 (CLS vs TRAJ parallel)\n- CodeRL, AlphaCode, Reflexion (verification-in-the-loop repair)\n- Predictive mutation testing literature (per-test binary classification precedent)\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WU9zu8QNnvpyfQcmhAeySK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"deepseek-cls-repo-v4\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest data, seed 42. 与 Qwen3 repo-level CLS 对标。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"accuracy\": 79.3,\n7\t      \"f1_macro\": 73.8,\n8\t      \"f1_fail\": 63.5,\n9\t      \"f1_pass\": 84.1,\n10\t      \"precision_fail\": 72.4,\n11\t      \"recall_fail\": 56.4,\n12\t      \"precision_pass\": 81.8,\n13\t      \"recall_pass\": 86.5,\n14\t      \"unparseable_pct\": 1.8,\n15\t      \"majority_baseline\": 73.0,\n16\t      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 6.3,\n17\t      \"total_samples\": 9784\n18\t    },\n19\t    \"tables\": [\n20\t      {\n21\t        \"name\": \"Table: DeepSeek vs Qwen3 Repo-Level CLS (seed 42)\",\n22\t        \"rows\": [\n23\t          {\n24\t            \"model\": \"Qwen3-4B\",\n25\t            \"accuracy\": 82.35,\n26\t            \"f1_macro\": 74.74,\n27\t            \"fail_f1\": 60.87\n28\t          },\n29\t          {\n30\t            \"model\": \"Qwen3-8B\",\n31\t            \"accuracy\": 84.79,\n32\t            \"f1_macro\": 81.18,\n33\t            \"fail_f1\": 72.93\n34\t          },\n35\t          {\n36\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-4B\",\n37\t            \"accuracy\": 79.3,\n38\t            \"f1_macro\": 73.8,\n39\t            \"fail_f1\": 63.5\n40\t          }\n41\t        ]\n42\t      }\n43\t    ],\n44\t    \"figures\": [],\n45\t    \"analysis\": \"DeepSeek CLS 低于 Qwen3 同规模 ~3pp，但仍高于 majority baseline 6.3pp。说明 CLS formulation 在不同 model family 上都可行，但绝对水平有差异。这支持 'design space is model-contingent' 叙事。\\n\\nDeepSeek tokenizer 对 repo-level 长序列处理能力与 Qwen3 不同。CLS 任务本身简单（binary），DeepSeek 应能达到合理水平但不如 Qwen3-4B 的 82-83%。原因：(1) DeepSeek base 在 code understanding 上略弱于 Qwen3 同规模，(2) repo-level 长上下文中 DeepSeek 的 attention pattern 不同导致 fail recall 偏低，(3) 但 format compliance 无问题（CLS 只需输出 pass/fail），unparseable 接近 0。与 Qwen3-4B ckpt-4600 的 82.35% 差 ~3pp，符合 median 档 'gap 较小' 预期。\"\n46\t  },\n47\t  {\n48\t    \"name\": \"deepseek-cls-repo-s123\",\n49\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level, seed 123. Multi-seed validation for DeepSeek repo CLS.\",\n50\t    \"results\": {\n51\t      \"accuracy\": 77.1,\n52\t      \"f1_macro\": 71.5,\n53\t      \"f1_fail\": 60.2,\n54\t      \"f1_pass\": 82.8,\n55\t      \"precision_fail\": 69.8,\n56\t      \"recall_fail\": 53.1,\n57\t      \"precision_pass\": 79.9,\n58\t      \"recall_pass\": 85.8,\n59\t      \"unparseable_pct\": 2.1,\n60\t      \"total_samples\": 9784\n61\t    },\n62\t    \"tables\": [],\n63\t    \"figures\": [],\n64\t    \"analysis\": \"两 seed 差异 2.2pp（79.3 vs 77.1），std ~1.6pp。相比 Qwen3 func-level 的 std 0.96pp，repo-level DeepSeek 的 variance 更大。需 hedge：'results are directionally consistent but seed-to-seed variation at repo-level is non-negligible'。\\n\\nSeed variance 在 DeepSeek repo-level 比 func-level 大（small test set effect + repo-level 难度高）。seed123 比 seed42 低 ~2pp，反映了 median 档 'seed variance 大' 的假设。两 seed 均值 ~78.2%，落在 [75,82] 范围内。这种 variance 使得统计显著性主张需要更多 seed 或 bootstrap CI，weakens any strong claim。\"\n65\t  },\n66\t  {\n67\t    \"name\": \"deepseek-cwm-repo\",\n68\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 42. 关键实验：验证 CWM unparseable 是否是 Qwen3 tokenizer-specific。\",\n69\t    \"results\": {\n70\t      \"accuracy\": 72.8,\n71\t      \"f1_macro\": 62.4,\n72\t      \"f1_fail\": 42.1,\n73\t      \"f1_pass\": 82.7,\n74\t      \"unparseable_pct\": 23.5,\n75\t      \"unparseable_count\": 2300,\n76\t      \"parseable_accuracy\": 78.6,\n77\t      \"exact_match_rate\": 31.2,\n78\t      \"precision_fail\": 55.3,\n79\t      \"recall_fail\": 33.9,\n80\t      \"precision_pass\": 76.8,\n81\t      \"recall_pass\": 89.4,\n82\t      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n83\t      \"majority_baseline\": 73.0,\n84\t      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": -0.2\n85\t    },\n86\t    \"tables\": [\n87\t      {\n88\t        \"name\": \"Table: CWM Unparseable Rate Comparison\",\n89\t        \"rows\": [\n90\t          {\n91\t            \"model\": \"Qwen3-4B func-level\",\n92\t            \"unparseable_pct\": 0,\n93\t            \"accuracy\": 87.51\n94\t          },\n95\t          {\n96\t            \"model\": \"Qwen3-4B repo-level\",\n97\t            \"unparseable_pct\": 93.0,\n98\t            \"accuracy\": 58.04\n99\t          },\n100\t          {\n101\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-4B func-level\",\n102\t            \"unparseable_pct\": 0,\n103\t            \"accuracy\": 85.77\n104\t          },\n105\t          {\n106\t            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-4B repo-level\",\n107\t            \"unparseable_pct\": 23.5,\n108\t            \"accuracy\": 72.8\n109\t          }\n110\t        ]\n111\t      }\n112\t    ],\n113\t    \"figures\": [],\n114\t    \"analysis\": \"CWM unparseable 从 Qwen3 的 93% 降至 DeepSeek 的 23.5%（-69.5pp），强力支持 'tokenizer-specific failure' claim。但 23.5% 仍不可忽略，说明 repo-level CWM 固有难度。CLS-CWM gap 6.5pp 在 parseable-only 上缩小到 0.7pp，进一步证明差异主要来自 format compliance 而非理解能力。\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：DeepSeek CWM unparseable 15-40%，远低于 Qwen3 的 54-93%。这证明 CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。但 23.5% unparseable 仍然 non-trivial，导致 overall accuracy 被拉低至 majority baseline 附近。parseable subset 上 accuracy 78.6% 说明 CWM 在 DeepSeek 上'可以工作'但 format compliance 仍是瓶颈。gap vs CLS 约 6.5pp（79.3 vs 72.8），落在 [0,8] 范围内。这个结果 interpretable（方向明确：CLS > CWM）但 not decisive（gap 可能被 unparseable handling 策略影响）。\"\n115\t  },\n116\t  {\n117\t    \"name\": \"deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\",\n118\t    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 123.\",\n119\t    \"results\": {\n120\t      \"accuracy\": 69.4,\n121\t      \"f1_macro\": 58.9,\n122\t      \"f1_fail\": 37.6,\n123\t      \"f1_pass\": 80.2,\n124\t      \"unparseable_pct\": 28.7,\n125\t      \"unparseable_count\": 2808,\n126\t      \"parseable_accuracy\": 75.3,\n127\t      \"exact_match_rate\": 28.9,\n128\t      \"total_samples\": 9784\n129\t    },\n130\t    \"tables\": [],\n131\t    \"figures\": [],\n132\t    \"analysis\": \"DeepSeek CWM 两 seed 差 3.4pp（72.8 vs 69.4），unparseable 差 5.2pp。variance 大于 CLS（2.2pp），符合 generation task 固有 instability。如果取 mean，CLS-CWM gap ~7pp，但 CI 很宽。写法需要：'CLS outperforms CWM on DeepSeek by 5-9pp depending on seed, though the gap is smaller than on Qwen3 (19-26pp) and primarily attributable to format compliance'。\\n\\nCWM generation 对 seed 更敏感（generation diversity → format compliance variance）。seed123 unparseable 比 seed42 高 5pp（28.7% vs 23.5%），导致 accuracy 再降 3.4pp。这种 high variance 是 median 档特征：'结果方向明确但 seed variance 大'。两 seed 均值 accuracy ~71.1%，CLS-CWM gap 均值 ~7.1pp。p-value 对这个 gap 在 2 seeds 下 likely 不显著（n=2 paired），需要更多 seed 或换 bootstrap。\"\n133\t  },\n134\t  {\n135\t    \"name\": \"swebench-pertest-data\",\n136\t    \"description\": \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test labels. 500 instances × 16 candidates.\",\n137\t    \"results\": {\n138\t      \"instances_completed\": 467,\n139\t      \"instances_failed_docker\": 33,\n140\t      \"total_test_pairs\": 74720,\n141\t      \"avg_tests_per_instance\": 10.0,\n142\t      \"avg_candidates_per_instance\": 16,\n143\t      \"pass_rate_gold\": 0.98,\n144\t      \"pass_rate_mutant\": 0.52,\n145\t      \"docker_timeout_pct\": 4.2,\n146\t      \"wall_clock_hours\": 22,\n147\t      \"parallel_containers\": 16\n148\t    },\n149\t    \"tables\": [],\n150\t    \"figures\": [],\n151\t    \"analysis\": \"Data construction step，无 accuracy 结论。467 instances 足以支撑后续 repo-level 训练（已有 repo-level-cls-v5 用此数据）。缺失的 33 instances 不影响 representativeness（random failure，非 systematic bias）。\\n\\n500 instances 中约 33 个 Docker 环境构建失败（dependency issues, deprecated packages），这在 SWE-bench 社区经验中正常（~6-7% failure rate）。467 个成功 instance 足以构建 dataset。per-test label extraction 本身是 deterministic（run test, check exit code），无 noise。主要 overhead 是 Docker build time 和 test suite execution time，16 parallel containers 下约 22h。\"\n152\t  },\n153\t  {\n154\t    \"name\": \"diagnostic-rerepair\",\n155\t    \"description\": \"Downstream POC: repair agent with per-test failure predictions vs no info. 200 instances, SWE-agent style.\",\n156\t    \"results\": {\n157\t      \"control_resolve_rate\": 0.22,\n158\t      \"cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate\": 0.27,\n159\t      \"oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate\": 0.32,\n160\t      \"random_diagnostic_resolve_rate\": 0.24,\n161\t      \"delta_cls_vs_control_pp\": 5.0,\n162\t      \"delta_oracle_vs_cls_pp\": 5.0,\n163\t      \"delta_random_vs_control_pp\": 2.0,\n164\t      \"n_instances\": 200,\n165\t      \"p_value_cls_vs_control\": 0.078,\n166\t      \"ci_95_lower_cls_delta\": -0.5,\n167\t      \"ci_95_upper_cls_delta\": 10.5,\n168\t      \"prompt_format_1_delta\": 7.0,\n169\t      \"prompt_format_2_delta\": 3.0\n170\t    },\n171\t    \"tables\": [\n172\t      {\n173\t        \"name\": \"Table: Re-repair Resolve Rate by Condition\",\n174\t        \"rows\": [\n175\t          {\n176\t            \"condition\": \"A1-control (no diagnostic)\",\n177\t            \"resolve_rate\": 0.22,\n178\t            \"n\": 200\n179\t          },\n180\t          {\n181\t            \"condition\": \"B-CLS diagnostic\",\n182\t            \"resolve_rate\": 0.27,\n183\t            \"n\": 200\n184\t          },\n185\t          {\n186\t            \"condition\": \"C-Oracle diagnostic\",\n187\t            \"resolve_rate\": 0.32,\n188\t            \"n\": 200\n189\t          },\n190\t          {\n191\t            \"condition\": \"D-Random diagnostic\",\n192\t            \"resolve_rate\": 0.24,\n193\t            \"n\": 200\n194\t          }\n195\t        ],\n196\t        \"caption\": \"Resolve rate (pass@1). p(B>A1)=0.078, McNemar paired test.\"\n197\t      }\n198\t    ],\n199\t    \"figures\": [],\n200\t    \"analysis\": \"5pp improvement 在方向上支持 diagnostic utility，但 p=0.078 不满足 conventional significance。Random (D) 的 2pp lift 说明 'any feedback helps' confound 存在。写法：'CLS-guided re-repair shows a trend toward higher resolve rate (+5pp, p=0.078), though the effect does not reach statistical significance at α=0.05 in our 200-instance evaluation. We note that even random test feedback provides marginal benefit (+2pp), suggesting the advantage is partially attributable to providing any per-test context rather than CLS-specific diagnostics.' 这足以回应 'no downstream utility' concern，但不能作为 core claim。\\n\\nMedian 档预期 CLS-diagnostic (B) 比 control (A1) 提升 3-8pp，统计显著性边缘。这里取 5pp（22% → 27%）。基线 22% resolve rate 合理（SWE-bench 上 open-source agent 通常 20-30%）。Oracle (C) 比 B 高 5pp（27% → 32%），说明 diagnostic info 有 room for improvement 但 CLS predictions 已捕捉大部分 signal。Random (D) 也有 2pp 提升（24%），这是 median 档的关键 'dilution' 因素：即使 random test feedback 也有些价值（给 agent 任何额外 context 都有帮助），稀释了 CLS-specific 贡献。p=0.078 边缘不显著（n=200, paired McNemar），CI 包含 0。两种 prompt format 效果不一致（7pp vs 3pp），robustness check 不完全通过。\"\n201\t  },\n202\t  {\n203\t    \"name\": \"re-repair-phase1-instruct\",\n204\t    \"description\": \"Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct, 60 instances, 5 conditions (A1/A2/B/C/D), Docker eval, 2 prompt formats.\",\n205\t    \"results\": {\n206\t      \"n_instances\": 60,\n207\t      \"conditions\": {\n208\t        \"A1_minimal\": {\n209\t          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.2,\n210\t          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.22,\n211\t          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.21\n212\t        },\n213\t        \"A2_test_names\": {\n214\t          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.23,\n215\t          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.23,\n216\t          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.23\n217\t        },\n218\t        \"B_cls_diagnostic\": {\n219\t          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.28,\n220\t          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.24,\n221\t          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.26\n222\t        },\n223\t        \"C_oracle_diagnostic\": {\n224\t          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.33,\n225\t          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.3,\n226\t          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.315\n227\t        },\n228\t        \"D_random_diagnostic\": {\n229\t          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.25,\n230\t          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.22,\n231\t          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.235\n232\t        }\n233\t      },\n234\t      \"delta_B_vs_A1_pp\": 5.0,\n235\t      \"delta_C_vs_B_pp\": 5.5,\n236\t      \"delta_B_vs_D_pp\": 2.5,\n237\t      \"delta_A2_vs_A1_pp\": 2.0,\n238\t      \"p_value_B_vs_A1\": 0.092,\n239\t      \"p_value_C_vs_A1\": 0.018,\n240\t      \"robustness_format1_passes\": true,\n241\t      \"robustness_format2_passes\": false,\n242\t      \"pass_at_5\": {\n243\t        \"A1\": 0.35,\n244\t        \"B\": 0.42,\n245\t        \"C\": 0.48,\n246\t        \"D\": 0.37\n247\t      }\n248\t    },\n249\t    \"tables\": [\n250\t      {\n251\t        \"name\": \"Table: Re-repair Phase 1 Results (Qwen3-8B-Instruct, N=60)\",\n252\t        \"rows\": [\n253\t          {\n254\t            \"condition\": \"A1-minimal\",\n255\t            \"format1\": 0.2,\n256\t            \"format2\": 0.22,\n257\t            \"mean\": 0.21\n258\t          },\n259\t          {\n260\t            \"condition\": \"A2-test-names\",\n261\t            \"format1\": 0.23,\n262\t            \"format2\": 0.23,\n263\t            \"mean\": 0.23\n264\t          },\n265\t          {\n266\t            \"condition\": \"B-CLS-diag\",\n267\t            \"format1\": 0.28,\n268\t            \"format2\": 0.24,\n269\t            \"mean\": 0.26\n270\t          },\n271\t          {\n272\t            \"condition\": \"C-Oracle-diag\",\n273\t            \"format1\": 0.33,\n274\t            \"format2\": 0.3,\n275\t            \"mean\": 0.315\n276\t          },\n277\t          {\n278\t            \"condition\": \"D-Random-diag\",\n279\t            \"format1\": 0.25,\n280\t            \"format2\": 0.22,\n281\t            \"mean\": 0.235\n282\t          }\n283\t        ]\n284\t      },\n285\t      {\n286\t        \"name\": \"Table: Statistical Tests\",\n287\t        \"rows\": [\n288\t          {\n289\t            \"comparison\": \"B vs A1\",\n290\t            \"delta_pp\": 5.0,\n291\t            \"p_value\": 0.092,\n292\t            \"significant\": \"no (α=0.05)\"\n293\t          },\n294\t          {\n295\t            \"comparison\": \"C vs A1\",\n296\t            \"delta_pp\": 10.5,\n297\t            \"p_value\": 0.018,\n298\t            \"significant\": \"yes\"\n299\t          },\n300\t          {\n301\t            \"comparison\": \"B vs D\",\n302\t            \"delta_pp\": 2.5,\n303\t            \"p_value\": 0.34,\n304\t            \"significant\": \"no\"\n305\t          },\n306\t          {\n307\t            \"comparison\": \"C vs B\",\n308\t            \"delta_pp\": 5.5,\n309\t            \"p_value\": 0.065,\n310\t            \"significant\": \"no (marginal)\"\n311\t          }\n312\t        ]\n313\t      }\n314\t    ],\n315\t    \"figures\": [],\n316\t    \"analysis\": \"Oracle (C) 显著优于 control 证明 per-test diagnostic information 有 intrinsic value for re-repair。但 CLS (B) 与 control 的差异不够显著（p=0.092），且 B vs D 差异更小（p=0.34），意味着 CLS prediction quality（87.5% accuracy）不足以完全 unlock 这个 value — 当 CLS 预测错误时反而 misleads agent。写法建议：'Oracle-guided re-repair significantly outperforms the control (p=0.018), establishing that per-test diagnostic information has downstream utility. CLS-guided re-repair shows a positive trend (+5pp) but does not reach significance, suggesting that prediction accuracy is a bottleneck for realizing the full potential of diagnostic-guided repair.' 这 honestly frames the limitation while still demonstrating the concept。\\n\\n60 instances 比 200 instances 方案更现实但 power 更低。Median 档核心特征：(1) B vs A1 +5pp 但 p=0.092（n=60 太小，McNemar power 不足），(2) C vs A1 +10.5pp 显著（p=0.018），证明 oracle diagnostic 有 clear value，(3) B vs D 仅 +2.5pp，CLS-specific contribution 被稀释，(4) Format 1 效果明显（B=28%）但 Format 2 退化（B=24%），robustness 不通过。A2（test names only）比 A1 高 2pp 说明即使只给 test name 也有些帮助，进一步稀释了 per-test pass/fail prediction 的 exclusive contribution。pass@5 差距更大（A1:35% vs B:42%），suggestion that diagnostic info helps exploration diversity。\"\n317\t  }\n318\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a235da8-f9b2-40e9-885f-aa66b75ac7cf","uuid":"1b601cb3-4f31-4d34-8a34-b041a01fc22e","timestamp":"2026-05-17T03:54:27.171Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_16/projects/exec-sim-repair-verifier/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T034206/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"deepseek-cls-repo-v4\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level SWE-bench-PerTest data, seed 42. 与 Qwen3 repo-level CLS 对标。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy\": 79.3,\n      \"f1_macro\": 73.8,\n      \"f1_fail\": 63.5,\n      \"f1_pass\": 84.1,\n      \"precision_fail\": 72.4,\n      \"recall_fail\": 56.4,\n      \"precision_pass\": 81.8,\n      \"recall_pass\": 86.5,\n      \"unparseable_pct\": 1.8,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 73.0,\n      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": 6.3,\n      \"total_samples\": 9784\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DeepSeek vs Qwen3 Repo-Level CLS (seed 42)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen3-4B\",\n            \"accuracy\": 82.35,\n            \"f1_macro\": 74.74,\n            \"fail_f1\": 60.87\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            \"accuracy\": 84.79,\n            \"f1_macro\": 81.18,\n            \"fail_f1\": 72.93\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-4B\",\n            \"accuracy\": 79.3,\n            \"f1_macro\": 73.8,\n            \"fail_f1\": 63.5\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DeepSeek CLS 低于 Qwen3 同规模 ~3pp，但仍高于 majority baseline 6.3pp。说明 CLS formulation 在不同 model family 上都可行，但绝对水平有差异。这支持 'design space is model-contingent' 叙事。\\n\\nDeepSeek tokenizer 对 repo-level 长序列处理能力与 Qwen3 不同。CLS 任务本身简单（binary），DeepSeek 应能达到合理水平但不如 Qwen3-4B 的 82-83%。原因：(1) DeepSeek base 在 code understanding 上略弱于 Qwen3 同规模，(2) repo-level 长上下文中 DeepSeek 的 attention pattern 不同导致 fail recall 偏低，(3) 但 format compliance 无问题（CLS 只需输出 pass/fail），unparseable 接近 0。与 Qwen3-4B ckpt-4600 的 82.35% 差 ~3pp，符合 median 档 'gap 较小' 预期。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"deepseek-cls-repo-s123\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CLS on repo-level, seed 123. Multi-seed validation for DeepSeek repo CLS.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy\": 77.1,\n      \"f1_macro\": 71.5,\n      \"f1_fail\": 60.2,\n      \"f1_pass\": 82.8,\n      \"precision_fail\": 69.8,\n      \"recall_fail\": 53.1,\n      \"precision_pass\": 79.9,\n      \"recall_pass\": 85.8,\n      \"unparseable_pct\": 2.1,\n      \"total_samples\": 9784\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"两 seed 差异 2.2pp（79.3 vs 77.1），std ~1.6pp。相比 Qwen3 func-level 的 std 0.96pp，repo-level DeepSeek 的 variance 更大。需 hedge：'results are directionally consistent but seed-to-seed variation at repo-level is non-negligible'。\\n\\nSeed variance 在 DeepSeek repo-level 比 func-level 大（small test set effect + repo-level 难度高）。seed123 比 seed42 低 ~2pp，反映了 median 档 'seed variance 大' 的假设。两 seed 均值 ~78.2%，落在 [75,82] 范围内。这种 variance 使得统计显著性主张需要更多 seed 或 bootstrap CI，weakens any strong claim。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"deepseek-cwm-repo\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 42. 关键实验：验证 CWM unparseable 是否是 Qwen3 tokenizer-specific。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy\": 72.8,\n      \"f1_macro\": 62.4,\n      \"f1_fail\": 42.1,\n      \"f1_pass\": 82.7,\n      \"unparseable_pct\": 23.5,\n      \"unparseable_count\": 2300,\n      \"parseable_accuracy\": 78.6,\n      \"exact_match_rate\": 31.2,\n      \"precision_fail\": 55.3,\n      \"recall_fail\": 33.9,\n      \"precision_pass\": 76.8,\n      \"recall_pass\": 89.4,\n      \"total_samples\": 9784,\n      \"majority_baseline\": 73.0,\n      \"gap_vs_majority_pp\": -0.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: CWM Unparseable Rate Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen3-4B func-level\",\n            \"unparseable_pct\": 0,\n            \"accuracy\": 87.51\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen3-4B repo-level\",\n            \"unparseable_pct\": 93.0,\n            \"accuracy\": 58.04\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-4B func-level\",\n            \"unparseable_pct\": 0,\n            \"accuracy\": 85.77\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeepSeek-4B repo-level\",\n            \"unparseable_pct\": 23.5,\n            \"accuracy\": 72.8\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CWM unparseable 从 Qwen3 的 93% 降至 DeepSeek 的 23.5%（-69.5pp），强力支持 'tokenizer-specific failure' claim。但 23.5% 仍不可忽略，说明 repo-level CWM 固有难度。CLS-CWM gap 6.5pp 在 parseable-only 上缩小到 0.7pp，进一步证明差异主要来自 format compliance 而非理解能力。\\n\\nMedian 档核心假设：DeepSeek CWM unparseable 15-40%，远低于 Qwen3 的 54-93%。这证明 CWM failure 是 tokenizer-specific 而非 formulation-inherent。但 23.5% unparseable 仍然 non-trivial，导致 overall accuracy 被拉低至 majority baseline 附近。parseable subset 上 accuracy 78.6% 说明 CWM 在 DeepSeek 上'可以工作'但 format compliance 仍是瓶颈。gap vs CLS 约 6.5pp（79.3 vs 72.8），落在 [0,8] 范围内。这个结果 interpretable（方向明确：CLS > CWM）但 not decisive（gap 可能被 unparseable handling 策略影响）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"deepseek-cwm-repo-s123\",\n    \"description\": \"DeepSeek-R1-0528 4B LoRA CWM generation on repo-level, seed 123.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"accuracy\": 69.4,\n      \"f1_macro\": 58.9,\n      \"f1_fail\": 37.6,\n      \"f1_pass\": 80.2,\n      \"unparseable_pct\": 28.7,\n      \"unparseable_count\": 2808,\n      \"parseable_accuracy\": 75.3,\n      \"exact_match_rate\": 28.9,\n      \"total_samples\": 9784\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DeepSeek CWM 两 seed 差 3.4pp（72.8 vs 69.4），unparseable 差 5.2pp。variance 大于 CLS（2.2pp），符合 generation task 固有 instability。如果取 mean，CLS-CWM gap ~7pp，但 CI 很宽。写法需要：'CLS outperforms CWM on DeepSeek by 5-9pp depending on seed, though the gap is smaller than on Qwen3 (19-26pp) and primarily attributable to format compliance'。\\n\\nCWM generation 对 seed 更敏感（generation diversity → format compliance variance）。seed123 unparseable 比 seed42 高 5pp（28.7% vs 23.5%），导致 accuracy 再降 3.4pp。这种 high variance 是 median 档特征：'结果方向明确但 seed variance 大'。两 seed 均值 accuracy ~71.1%，CLS-CWM gap 均值 ~7.1pp。p-value 对这个 gap 在 2 seeds 下 likely 不显著（n=2 paired），需要更多 seed 或换 bootstrap。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"swebench-pertest-data\",\n    \"description\": \"Docker re-evaluation of SWE-bench Verified patches to extract per-test labels. 500 instances × 16 candidates.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"instances_completed\": 467,\n      \"instances_failed_docker\": 33,\n      \"total_test_pairs\": 74720,\n      \"avg_tests_per_instance\": 10.0,\n      \"avg_candidates_per_instance\": 16,\n      \"pass_rate_gold\": 0.98,\n      \"pass_rate_mutant\": 0.52,\n      \"docker_timeout_pct\": 4.2,\n      \"wall_clock_hours\": 22,\n      \"parallel_containers\": 16\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Data construction step，无 accuracy 结论。467 instances 足以支撑后续 repo-level 训练（已有 repo-level-cls-v5 用此数据）。缺失的 33 instances 不影响 representativeness（random failure，非 systematic bias）。\\n\\n500 instances 中约 33 个 Docker 环境构建失败（dependency issues, deprecated packages），这在 SWE-bench 社区经验中正常（~6-7% failure rate）。467 个成功 instance 足以构建 dataset。per-test label extraction 本身是 deterministic（run test, check exit code），无 noise。主要 overhead 是 Docker build time 和 test suite execution time，16 parallel containers 下约 22h。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"diagnostic-rerepair\",\n    \"description\": \"Downstream POC: repair agent with per-test failure predictions vs no info. 200 instances, SWE-agent style.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"control_resolve_rate\": 0.22,\n      \"cls_diagnostic_resolve_rate\": 0.27,\n      \"oracle_diagnostic_resolve_rate\": 0.32,\n      \"random_diagnostic_resolve_rate\": 0.24,\n      \"delta_cls_vs_control_pp\": 5.0,\n      \"delta_oracle_vs_cls_pp\": 5.0,\n      \"delta_random_vs_control_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"n_instances\": 200,\n      \"p_value_cls_vs_control\": 0.078,\n      \"ci_95_lower_cls_delta\": -0.5,\n      \"ci_95_upper_cls_delta\": 10.5,\n      \"prompt_format_1_delta\": 7.0,\n      \"prompt_format_2_delta\": 3.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Re-repair Resolve Rate by Condition\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"A1-control (no diagnostic)\",\n            \"resolve_rate\": 0.22,\n            \"n\": 200\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"B-CLS diagnostic\",\n            \"resolve_rate\": 0.27,\n            \"n\": 200\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"C-Oracle diagnostic\",\n            \"resolve_rate\": 0.32,\n            \"n\": 200\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"D-Random diagnostic\",\n            \"resolve_rate\": 0.24,\n            \"n\": 200\n          }\n        ],\n        \"caption\": \"Resolve rate (pass@1). p(B>A1)=0.078, McNemar paired test.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"5pp improvement 在方向上支持 diagnostic utility，但 p=0.078 不满足 conventional significance。Random (D) 的 2pp lift 说明 'any feedback helps' confound 存在。写法：'CLS-guided re-repair shows a trend toward higher resolve rate (+5pp, p=0.078), though the effect does not reach statistical significance at α=0.05 in our 200-instance evaluation. We note that even random test feedback provides marginal benefit (+2pp), suggesting the advantage is partially attributable to providing any per-test context rather than CLS-specific diagnostics.' 这足以回应 'no downstream utility' concern，但不能作为 core claim。\\n\\nMedian 档预期 CLS-diagnostic (B) 比 control (A1) 提升 3-8pp，统计显著性边缘。这里取 5pp（22% → 27%）。基线 22% resolve rate 合理（SWE-bench 上 open-source agent 通常 20-30%）。Oracle (C) 比 B 高 5pp（27% → 32%），说明 diagnostic info 有 room for improvement 但 CLS predictions 已捕捉大部分 signal。Random (D) 也有 2pp 提升（24%），这是 median 档的关键 'dilution' 因素：即使 random test feedback 也有些价值（给 agent 任何额外 context 都有帮助），稀释了 CLS-specific 贡献。p=0.078 边缘不显著（n=200, paired McNemar），CI 包含 0。两种 prompt format 效果不一致（7pp vs 3pp），robustness check 不完全通过。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"re-repair-phase1-instruct\",\n    \"description\": \"Re-repair with Qwen3-8B-Instruct, 60 instances, 5 conditions (A1/A2/B/C/D), Docker eval, 2 prompt formats.\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_instances\": 60,\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"A1_minimal\": {\n          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.2,\n          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.22,\n          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.21\n        },\n        \"A2_test_names\": {\n          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.23,\n          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.23,\n          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.23\n        },\n        \"B_cls_diagnostic\": {\n          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.28,\n          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.24,\n          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.26\n        },\n        \"C_oracle_diagnostic\": {\n          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.33,\n          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.3,\n          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.315\n        },\n        \"D_random_diagnostic\": {\n          \"resolve_rate_format1\": 0.25,\n          \"resolve_rate_format2\": 0.22,\n          \"mean_resolve_rate\": 0.235\n        }\n      },\n      \"delta_B_vs_A1_pp\": 5.0,\n      \"delta_C_vs_B_pp\": 5.5,\n      \"delta_B_vs_D_pp\": 2.5,\n      \"delta_A2_vs_A1_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"p_value_B_vs_A1\": 0.092,\n      \"p_value_C_vs_A1\": 0.018,\n      \"robustness_format1_passes\": true,\n      \"robustness_format2_passes\": false,\n      \"pass_at_5\": {\n        \"A1\": 0.35,\n        \"B\": 0.42,\n        \"C\": 0.48,\n        \"D\": 0.37\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Re-repair Phase 1 Results (Qwen3-8B-Instruct, N=60)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"A1-minimal\",\n            \"format1\": 0.2,\n            \"format2\": 0.22,\n            \"mean\": 0.21\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"A2-test-names\",\n            \"format1\": 0.23,\n            \"format2\": 0.23,\n            \"mean\": 0.23\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"B-CLS-diag\",\n            \"format1\": 0.28,\n            \"format2\": 0.24,\n            \"mean\": 0.26\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"C-Oracle-diag\",\n            \"format1\": 0.33,\n            \"format2\": 0.3,\n            \"mean\": 0.315\n          },\n          {\n            \"condition\": \"D-Random-diag\",\n            \"format1\": 0.25,\n            \"format2\": 0.22,\n            \"mean\": 0.235\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Statistical Tests\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"comparison\": \"B vs A1\",\n            \"delta_pp\": 5.0,\n            \"p_value\": 0.092,\n            \"significant\": \"no (α=0.05)\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"comparison\": \"C vs A1\",\n            \"delta_pp\": 10.5,\n            \"p_value\": 0.018,\n            \"significant\": \"yes\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"comparison\": \"B vs D\",\n            \"delta_pp\": 2.5,\n            \"p_value\": 0.34,\n            \"significant\": \"no\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"comparison\": \"C vs B\",\n            \"delta_pp\": 5.5,\n            \"p_value\": 0.065,\n            \"significant\": \"no (marginal)\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Oracle (C) 显著优于 control 证明 per-test diagnostic information 有 intrinsic value for re-repair。但 CLS (B) 与 control 的差异不够显著（p=0.092），且 B vs D 差异更小（p=0.34），意味着 CLS prediction quality（87.5% accuracy）不足以完全 unlock 这个 value — 当 CLS 预测错误时反而 misleads agent。写法建议：'Oracle-guided re-repair significantly outperforms the control (p=0.018), establishing that per-test diagnostic information has downstream utility. CLS-guided re-repair shows a positive trend (+5pp) but does not reach significance, suggesting that prediction accuracy is a bottleneck for realizing the full potential of diagnostic-guided repair.' 这 honestly frames the limitation while still demonstrating the concept。\\n\\n60 instances 比 200 instances 方案更现实但 power 更低。Median 档核心特征：(1) B vs A1 +5pp 但 p=0.092（n=60 太小，McNemar power 不足），(2) C vs A1 +10.5pp 显著（p=0.018），证明 oracle diagnostic 有 clear value，(3) B vs D 仅 +2.5pp，CLS-specific contribution 被稀释，(4) Format 1 效果明显（B=28%）但 Format 2 退化（B=24%），robustness 不通过。A2（test names only）比 A1 高 2pp 说明即使只给 test name 也有些帮助，进一步稀释了 per-test pass/fail prediction 的 exclusive contribution。pass@5 差距更大（A1:35% vs B:42%），suggestion that diagnostic info helps exploration diversity。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":318,"startLine":1,"totalLines":318}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015v9QiGvXwdwn3asok1rNMq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture. Let me write the paper. Key points from the data and framing:\n\n1. **Title**: Something about \"The Formulation Design Space for Neural Code Verification\" - an empirical study\n2. **Core claims**:\n   - Formulation equivalence at function-level\n   - Complexity-dependent divergence that is model-contingent\n   - Diagnostic granularity without accuracy cost\n3. **Experiments to cover**:\n   - deepseek-cls-repo-v4: DeepSeek CLS results, comparison with Qwen3\n   - Multi-seed validation across both CLS and CWM formulations\n   - CWM with DeepSeek, looking at unparseable rates\n   - Data construction for the swebench-pertest setup\n   - Re-repair as a proof-of-concept with 200 instances, then a more detailed phase 1 with 60 instances and specific conditions\n\n4. **Narrative guidance**: Re-repair as supplementary evidence, not core claim. Hedge language. Main claims are the three core claims. Target EMNLP Main, Findings as realistic landing.\n\nNow I'm planning the paper structure: Abstract, Introduction, Related Work, then the Method section covering the formulation design space with CLS, CWM, and TRAJ. For Experiments, I'll walk through data construction with SWE-bench PerTest, cross-model comparison between DeepSeek and Qwen3, unparseable rate analysis, multi-seed stability, and downstream utility through re-repair. I need to be careful to only use numbers from experiment_data.json and then check for the output directory.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2054,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6506,"cache_read_input_tokens":25034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6506},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"c